       "acrm---usecase-heading": "High Converting Landing Page Examples",
       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"High-Converting Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What are the best practices for creating high-converting landing pages?\", \"a\": \"Give the page one goal and one button, and build everything else around them. Match the headline to the ad or email that sent the visitor, ask only for the fields you will use, and put a named customer quote beside the form. Check the page on a phone before launch, then test one change at a time against the version that is live.\"}, {\"q\": \"How to build a high converting landing page?\", \"a\": \"Decide the one action you want and the fields the form needs, then describe both in a prompt to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder'>AI landing page builder</a>. It returns a working page with a leads table behind it. Submit a test lead yourself, check that the row arrived, and publish once the page reads clearly on a phone.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should I look for in high converting landing page examples?\", \"a\": \"Look for what changed and what the change did to the numbers. The high converting landing page examples worth copying say what was tested: a shorter form, a new headline, a quote moved next to the button. A screenshot with no before and after shows a style, and it cannot tell you whether that style will work for your visitors.\"}, {\"q\": \"What do high converting landing page templates get right?\", \"a\": \"They get the order right: a headline, a one-line promise, the form or button, proof, and then the details. Borrow that order from high converting landing page templates and rewrite every line for your own offer. A <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/webinar'>webinar landing page</a>, for instance, needs the date with its time zone and what attendees will learn above the signup button.\"}, {\"q\": \"How long should a high-converting landing page be?\", \"a\": \"It should be as long as a visitor needs to decide, and no longer. A free quote or a newsletter signup fits on one screen, with the form right under the headline and a line of proof beside it. A higher-priced offer needs room for pricing and objections. Add those sections below the first form and repeat the button after them.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I measure the conversion rate of a high-converting landing page?\", \"a\": \"Divide the conversions by the visitors who reached the page, then multiply by 100. Count only the action the page exists for. Measure each traffic source on its own, since ad clicks and newsletter readers arrive with different intent. On a page built with Emergent, every submission lands in your own leads table, where the count of new rows is the number to divide.\"}, {\"q\": \"What does a high-converting landing page need for business buyers?\", \"a\": \"It needs proof that a buyer can forward to colleagues, such as named customers and the problem each one solved, plus a next step like a demo. On a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/b2b'>b2b landing page</a>, ask for a work email and company size so larger accounts reach sales first. If IT signs off on purchases like yours, list the integrations and security answers they will ask for.\"}, {\"q\": \"How many form fields should a high-converting landing page have?\", \"a\": \"Ask for as few fields as you will act on, and treat three as the ceiling for a first contact. Save everything else for the thank-you screen or a follow-up email, after the lead is already in. The app Emergent builds saves every submission to a database you own, where a later answer from the same person can join their row.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I split test two versions of a high-converting landing page?\", \"a\": \"Show each visitor one of two versions, change only one element between them, and count conversions for each. Pick the metric before launch, such as demo requests, and wait until each version has a few hundred visitors before calling a winner. Emergent builds both versions and the split from a plain-English prompt, and a second prompt starts the next test.\"}, {\"q\": \"Why would a high-converting landing page convert worse on paid ad clicks?\", \"a\": \"Because the page does not repeat what the ad promised. A visitor who clicked an ad for one service and lands on a general page has to hunt for it. Give each ad group its own <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/ppc'>ppc landing page</a> with the ad's offer in the headline. With the button text and the form the same across those pages, the top line is the only difference.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
